    "Five failed summonses produce a request for Braun's compelled appearance";
!}

= 14 July 2026 — Procedure without a martyr script

<span class="party-korona"><b>Grzegorz Braun</b></span>, a Korona leader and member of the European Parliament, has
ignored five attempts to complete procedural acts in the separate Oleśnica
hospital investigation. Prosecutor General **[+ justice_minister +]** now asks
the European Parliament to permit Braun's detention long enough to compel an
appearance and hear the charges.

The request concerns six alleged offences, including unlawfully detaining and
making physical contact with a doctor at the hospital. It is not a request for
pre-trial imprisonment, nor is it a verdict in Braun's older seven-count
indictment. [? if braun_legal_preparation >= 8: Earlier documentation, victim
support and count-by-count explanations have left prosecutors a record capable
of surviving political scrutiny.?][? if braun_legal_preparation < 8: Earlier
preparation is thin, leaving Braun room to present several separate files as
one political prosecution.?] Lewica must defend equal process without writing
the martyrdom script for him.

- @braun_warrant
- @braun_surrender
- @braun_case_separation
- @braun_overreach

@braun_warrant
title: Support the immunity request and ordinary compelled appearance
subtitle: Ask Parliament to permit only what five ignored summonses now require, and no more.
on-arrival: {!
Q.braun_compulsion_strategy = "Ordinary compelled appearance";
Q.prosecution_command_clarity += 2;
Q.government_procedural_restraint += 3;
Q.constitutional_restraint += 3;
Q.braun_martyrdom += Q.braun_legal_preparation >= 8 ? 1 : 3;
Q.minority_safety += 2;
Q.news_headline =
    "The compulsion request is defended as ordinary criminal procedure";
!}

Lewica supports the European Parliament request as a narrow step toward an
ordinary interview under criminal procedure. Prosecutors must still prove each
allegation and justify every later restraint. Braun calls the vote political
persecution, but the demand remains stubbornly smaller than the grand trial he
wants to describe.

- @poland_event_queue: Back the request

@braun_surrender
title: Support one final written deadline before compulsion
subtitle: Give Braun a public date, place and consequence so that only his compliance remains in dispute.
on-arrival: braun_compulsion_strategy = "Final written deadline before compulsion"; government_procedural_restraint += 4; braun_martyrdom -= 2; public_trust += 2; prosecution_oversight_capacity += 1; braun_legal_preparation += 1; news_headline = "A final written deadline narrows the dispute to compliance with a summons"

The summons is published with a final date and a precise warning that compelled
appearance follows non-compliance. Victims wait longer, but Braun loses the
claim that an arrest came without an available lawful exit. When the deadline
expires, the European Parliament will be judging a documented refusal rather
than a cloud of prosecutorial rhetoric.

- @poland_event_queue: Publish the final summons

@braun_case_separation
title: Keep the hospital file, older indictment and speech cases visibly separate
subtitle: Give each complainant independent representation and deny Braun the single political trial he wants.
choose-if: braun_legal_preparation >= 8
unavailable-subtitle: Earlier choices did not build a sufficiently clear count-by-count record.
on-arrival: braun_compulsion_strategy = "Separate cases and independent victim representation"; braun_legal_preparation += 3; braun_martyrdom -= 3; public_trust += 2; minority_safety += 2; prosecution_oversight_capacity += 2; constitutional_restraint += 2; news_headline = "Separate files deny Braun one grand political trial"

Prosecutors publish separate chronologies, legal bases and victim contacts for
the Oleśnica file, the older indictment and speech-related cases. The hospital
doctor no longer disappears inside a national argument about Braun. His
supporters still allege persecution, but they must now answer several bounded
proceedings rather than one invented show trial.

- @poland_event_queue: Separate the files

@braun_overreach
title: Demand immediate pre-trial detention and a broad extremist case
subtitle: Collapse separate allegations into one political case and accept that the demand outruns the immunity request before Parliament.
on-arrival: braun_compulsion_strategy = "Pre-trial detention and one broad extremist case"; progressive_credibility += 2; government_procedural_restraint -= 5; braun_martyrdom += 8; braun_legal_preparation -= 3 if braun_legal_preparation >= 3; far_right_agenda += 5; public_trust -= 2; news_headline = "Political overstatement gives Braun the case he wanted to narrate"

Lewica demands imprisonment and a single extremist prosecution before the
European Parliament has authorised even compelled questioning. Braun places
the statement at the centre of his defence and invites every separate
allegation to shelter behind it. Victims gain a fierce declaration; prosecutors
inherit a political burden that their narrow request did not create.

- @poland_event_queue: Make the demand

@unia_centrum_2026
# prose-audit: Grade A — The losing Poland 2050 wing and Kobosko are introduced as the organisers behind a registered party, parliamentary seats are distinguished from a national machine, and every Lewica response changes a named relationship or governing arrangement on the page.
title: Unia Centrum becomes a political party
subtitle: The Poland 2050 breakaway acquires a name it can put on a ballot
face-image: img/poland/events/sejm-new-deputies-2023.webp
