on-arrival: unia_centrum_formed = 1; government_coalition_dissent += 3 if centrum_supports_government = 1; news_headline = "Unia Centrum turns a parliamentary split into an electoral competitor"

= July 2026 — Another party and another threshold

**[+ centrum_leader +]**, leader of the wing that lost Poland 2050's succession
fight, and former first vice-chair <span class="party-p2050"><b>Michał Kobosko</b></span> have registered **Unia
Centrum** as a political party. Its **[+ centrum_seats +] MPs** provide speaking
time, staff and committee votes; registration provides a name for a ballot.
Neither proves that the organisation has members and candidates across the
country.

[? if centrum_supports_government: The breakaway still supports the cabinet,
so each of those votes now belongs to a separate negotiating table. It holds no
ministry unless a recorded reshuffle grants one.?][? if not
centrum_supports_government: Unia Centrum sits outside the governing
arrangement. Lewica can coordinate votes and discuss lists, but cannot promise
the new party cabinet authority it does not possess.?] We can recognise it as
a bilateral partner, insist that both centrist heirs enter one democratic list,
or leave the breakaway to discover whether a Sejm caucus is an electorate.

- @centrum_bilateral
- @centrum_common
- @centrum_ignore

@centrum_bilateral
title: Negotiate a separate cooperation protocol with Unia Centrum
subtitle: Give Kobosko's caucus its own parliamentary channel and accept that Poland 2050 will read this as recognition of a rival.
on-arrival: centrum_relation = 48; p2050_relation -= 2; government_coalition_dissent += 2 if centrum_supports_government = 1; public_trust += 1; news_headline = "Lewica signs a bilateral parliamentary agreement with Unia Centrum"

Lewica and Unia Centrum publish a short protocol on committee work,
constitutional votes and consultation before confidence motions. [? if
centrum_supports_government: The cabinet gains a predictable channel but also a
new junior partner able to withhold its own votes.?][? if not
centrum_supports_government: The protocol coordinates two opposition clubs; it
does not make either one a ministerial party.?] Poland 2050 sees Lewica treating
its defectors as a permanent competitor.

- @poland_event_queue: Publish the protocol

@centrum_common
title: Offer a common democratic list if both centrist parties cooperate
subtitle: Offer threshold insurance to both heirs, but only through one joint list whose places must still be negotiated.
on-arrival: centrum_relation = 55; p2050_relation += 3; ko_relation -= 2; government_coalition_dissent -= 1 if centrum_supports_government = 1; local_network += 1; news_headline = "Threshold fear produces an early common-list proposal"

Lewica invites Unia Centrum and Poland 2050 to map one democratic list before
their rivalry becomes six local vetoes. Both parties welcome protection from an
electoral threshold and immediately dispute names, districts and order. KO
objects that Lewica is designing the centre's ballot without the largest
opposition organisation in the room.

- @poland_event_queue: Put the map to both parties

@centrum_ignore
title: Let the tiny party prove it has an electorate
subtitle: Offer no protocol and, if Unia Centrum supports the cabinet, stop counting its MPs as dependable government votes.
on-arrival: {!
const centrumWasSupporting = Boolean(Q.centrum_supports_government);
Q.centrum_relation = 25;
if (centrumWasSupporting) {
    Q.government_coalition_dissent += 4;
}
Q.public_trust -= 1;
Q.barons_dissent -= 1;
if (
    centrumWasSupporting && Q.government_has_confidence &&
    !Q.caretaker_government
) {
    Q.government_support_seats = Math.max(
        0,
        (Number(Q.government_support_seats) || 0) -
            (Number(Q.centrum_seats) || 0)
    );
}
Q.centrum_supports_government = 0;
Q.news_headline = centrumWasSupporting
    ? "Unia Centrum begins campaigning against its coalition partners"
    : "Unia Centrum begins campaigning against the other centrist parties";
!}

Lewica declines a separate agreement. Unia Centrum responds by campaigning
against both Poland 2050 and us as parties afraid of a new centre. [? if
centrum_withdrew_support_2026: Its **[+ centrum_seats +] MPs** leave the cabinet's
working count; survival must be demonstrated bill by bill.?][? if not
centrum_withdrew_support_2026: No government majority changes, but the breakaway
enters every future vote as a rival rather than a consulted partner.?] The new
party now has the independence it asked for and none of the organisational help
it hoped to borrow.

- @poland_event_queue: Decline the agreement

@centrum_club_settlement_2026
# prose-audit: Grade B — The losing wing and Kobosko remain named, a Sejm circle or club is distinguished from a registered party, and both reunion and autonomy receive exact parliamentary aftermaths; the event is deliberately a short organisational settlement.
title: Centrum remains a caucus without a party
subtitle: February produced MPs and staff, not the local machine needed to contest Poland
