= July 2026 — A club is not yet a party

**[+ centrum_leader +]** and former Poland 2050 first vice-chair **Michał
Kobosko** retain **[+ centrum_seats +] MPs**. [? if centrum_seats >= 15: That is
enough for a formal Sejm club.?][? if centrum_seats < 15: It is a parliamentary
circle, not the fifteen-member club that receives the Sejm's fuller rights.?]
Either form supplies a microphone, staff and committee work. It does not supply
a registered party, local candidates or a national electorate.

The orderly February separation left offices intact but gave the breakaway no
automatic machine. Lewica can broker reunion with Poland 2050 or recognise a
separate caucus without pretending that it can yet put an independent party on
the ballot.

- @centrum_reunite
- @centrum_remain_club

@centrum_reunite
title: Broker a return to Poland 2050 under autonomy guarantees
subtitle: The separate seats return to the parent club; dissent falls and no new party forms.
on-arrival: {!
const centrumSeatsReturning = Math.max(0, Number(Q.centrum_seats) || 0);
Q.centrum_returned_seats_2026 = centrumSeatsReturning;
const parentSupportsGovernment =
    Q.government_party == "p2050" || Boolean(Q.ministry_p2050_in_cabinet);
if (Q.centrum_supports_government && !parentSupportsGovernment) {
    Q.government_support_seats = Math.max(
        0,
        (Number(Q.government_support_seats) || 0) - centrumSeatsReturning
    );
}
Q.p2050_seats += centrumSeatsReturning;
Q.centrum_seats = 0;
Q.p2050_split = 0;
Q.centrum_supports_government = 0;
Q.p2050_coalition_dissent -= 7;
Q.p2050_relation += 4;
Q.centrum_relation += 2;
Q.centrum_party_readiness = 0;
Q.centrum_independent_vote_base = 0;
Q.news_headline =
    "The centrist caucus reunites under an autonomy agreement";
!}

The two wings sign guarantees for regional nominations, internal votes and a
place for Kobosko's network in the reunited organisation. All **[+
centrum_returned_seats_2026 +]** mandates have already been transferred back to Poland 2050
in the Sejm count; Centrum's separate caucus and electoral claim end here.
Autonomy survives on paper, ready to become either a bridge or the terms of the
next quarrel.

- @poland_event_queue: Sign the autonomy guarantees

@centrum_remain_club
title: Recognise a separate caucus without manufacturing a party
subtitle: Give its MPs a parliamentary channel while leaving registration, members and ballot access to their own work.
on-arrival: centrum_relation += 4; government_coalition_dissent += 2 if centrum_supports_government = 1; centrum_party_readiness += 1; public_trust += 1; news_headline = "Centrum remains a separate parliamentary caucus"

Lewica treats Centrum's MPs as a distinct caucus in committee negotiations and
leaders' meetings. [? if centrum_supports_government: That recognition creates
one more coalition veto point without awarding a ministry.?][? if not
centrum_supports_government: It creates a parliamentary interlocutor, not a new
governing partner.?] Kobosko gains time and visibility; whether those resources
become a party remains his organisation's burden.

- @poland_event_queue: Recognise the caucus

