@airspace_incident_2026
# prose-audit: Grade C — The single incident is correctly written as one entry in an accumulating record rather than as news, and the three answers separate readiness, politics and civil protection; the affected village is not yet a place.
title: Another object comes down in the east
subtitle: One more incident in a record the state has stopped counting properly
face-image: img/poland/events/polish-f16.webp
new-page: true
tags: poland_event
priority: 26
order: 25
max-visits: 1
view-if: continuous_campaign = 1 and year = 2026 and month = 7 and airspace_incident_2026_done = 0
on-arrival: {!
Q.airspace_incident_2026_done = 1;
Q.security_incident_pressure =
    (Number(Q.security_incident_pressure) || 0) + 12;
const incidents = Number(Q.security_incident_pressure) || 0;
Q.security_incident_record = incidents >= 40
    ? "a continuous pattern the public now expects to repeat"
    : (incidents >= 20
        ? "a recognisable series rather than a set of accidents"
        : "a short list that has not yet become a pattern");
Q.defence_readiness = Math.max(
    0, (Number(Q.defence_readiness) || 50) - 4
);
Q.news_headline =
    "Debris from an unidentified aerial object is found in eastern Poland";
!}

= July 2026 — The record, not the object

Fragments of an aerial object come down on farmland in the east. The military
says it poses no danger and does not say what it was; residents photographed
it before any uniform arrived; the identification takes days and satisfies
nobody. It may have been a Russian missile, a drone, or debris from an
interception over Ukraine.

The individual answer matters less than the accumulation. Together with the
drone incursions, the border incidents, the railway sabotage attempts and the
espionage arrests of the previous years, this is **[+
security_incident_record +]**. There is still no single public register, no
routine notification to the municipalities involved, and no standing
explanation of what a resident is supposed to do when something lands in a
field.

[? if defence_command_response = "Operational record demanded" or defence_command_response = "Brokered continuity statement" or defence_command_response = "Joint opposition demand": We
asked the command-continuity question in October 2023 and were told it was a
campaign stunt. The file we opened then is the only continuous record anybody
has of who was answerable for what.?]
[? if defence_command_response = "Closing competence attack": We turned the
2023 command resignations into a campaign argument, and the services have been
saying less to everybody ever since.?]
[? if left_in_government = 1: The interior and defence ministries in this
cabinet own the notification failure, whatever they own of the incident
itself.?][? if left_in_government = 0: We hold nothing here except the ability
to insist that the pattern be counted in public.?]

- @airspace_register
- @airspace_civil_protection
- @airspace_blame
- @poland_events_2026_snap.airspace_standing_review

@airspace_register
title: Demand a single public register of every incident since 2022
subtitle: Makes the pattern legible and forces the state to admit how much of it went unrecorded.
on-arrival: {!
Q.airspace_response = "Public incident register";
Q.security_incident_pressure = Math.max(
    0, (Number(Q.security_incident_pressure) || 0) - 6
);
Q.defence_readiness =
    (Number(Q.defence_readiness) || 46) + 4;
Q.civil_military_trust =
    (Number(Q.civil_military_trust) || 50) + 3;
Q.institutional_trust =
    (Number(Q.institutional_trust) || 0) + 4;
Q.administrative_reform_pressure =
    (Number(Q.administrative_reform_pressure) || 0) + 3;
Q.public_trust = (Number(Q.public_trust) || 0) + 2;
Q.news_headline =
    "One published register replaces four years of separate announcements";
!}

One register: date, location, object, who identified it, how long it took, and
what the residents were told. Everything already exists in fragments across
three ministries; the demand is only that it be published in one place and
kept current.

It is an unheroic request that changes the argument permanently, because a
pattern that is written down can be governed, and one that is announced
incident by incident can only be reacted to. The first version of the register
is embarrassing to everyone who has held the portfolios since 2022.

- @poland_event_queue: Demand the register

@airspace_civil_protection
title: Fund municipal civil protection and a standing notification duty
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource. Puts money and a legal duty where the debris actually lands.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: The party cannot staff a civil-protection proposal this month.
on-arrival: {!
Q.resources = (Number(Q.resources) || 0) - 1;
Q.airspace_response = "Municipal civil protection";
Q.defence_readiness =
    (Number(Q.defence_readiness) || 46) + 3;
Q.administrative_capacity = (Number(Q.administrative_capacity) || 0) +
    (Q.left_in_government ? 3 : 0);
Q.local_network = (Number(Q.local_network) || 0) + 3;
Q.rural_support = (Number(Q.rural_support) || 0) + 3;
Q.institutional_trust =
    (Number(Q.institutional_trust) || 0) + 3;
Q.public_trust = (Number(Q.public_trust) || 0) + 3;
Q.security_incident_pressure = Math.max(
    0, (Number(Q.security_incident_pressure) || 0) - 4
);
Q.news_headline =
    "Border municipalities get a notification duty and money to answer it";
!}

The proposal is written for the village rather than the general staff: a legal
duty to notify the commune within a stated number of hours, a funded local
contact, and a published instruction that an ordinary person can follow when
something is smoking in their field.

It is the least dramatic security policy available and the only one that
reaches the people who keep finding these objects first. Local councils across
the eastern belt — including several the Left has never won — respond to it
directly.

- @poland_event_queue: Fund the municipal duty

@airspace_blame
title: Make it a competence charge against whoever holds the defence ministry
subtitle: The obvious political use of the incident; it teaches the services to say less next time.
on-arrival: airspace_response = "Competence attack"; civil_military_trust -= 6; security_incident_pressure += 4; left_poll_momentum += 0.15; public_trust += 1; institutional_trust -= 3; defence_readiness -= 2; public_mood_pending_national_security_salience += 9; public_mood_pending_national_security_support += -4; news_headline = "The debris becomes an argument about who runs the defence ministry"

Four years of incidents and the state still cannot say what fell on a farm for
three days. The charge is fair, it lands, and the ministry has no answer that
is not a classification notice.

The services draw the obvious conclusion, which is that every future
identification should be slower, vaguer and cleared further up the chain
before anyone says anything. The next village waits longer.

- @poland_event_queue: Press the competence charge
